# /etc/paperbot/executor-toobit.env  (root:root, chmod 600; made by install.sh from this template, filled by an owner)
# The keys of the Toobit account (owners 10-25, docs/toobit-ko.md: the $50 executor paperbot-executor-toobit). systemd
# reads this file for that one unit INSTEAD of /etc/paperbot/executor.env, so the other executors and this one never see
# each other's keys. Never commit the real file, never paste a key in a chat: write it on the server with
#   sudoedit /etc/paperbot/executor-toobit.env
#
# Only the lines below. Do NOT start from a copy of /etc/paperbot/executor.env: the executor ("own_keys": true) refuses
# to start when another exchange's key (BYBIT_*, MEXC_*, WOOXPRO_*, DEEPCOIN_* ...) is in its environment.
#
# Toobit: a key made in the account (API management) with the futures trade permission only, NO withdrawal, bound to
# this server's IP 158.247.200.152; the API key and the secret key (shown once when the key is made).
TOOBIT_LIVE_KEY=
TOOBIT_LIVE_SECRET=
# Toobit cannot report a key's permissions through the API: after checking the key page (futures trade only, no
# withdrawal, IP bound), write exactly FUTURES_ONLY_NO_WITHDRAW_IP_BOUND here (the executor refuses to start without it)
TOOBIT_LIVE_KEY_CHECKED=
# The mainnet switch: exactly I_UNDERSTAND, and only together with "mode": "mainnet" in executor-toobit.json.
PAPERBOT_LIVE_MAINNET=
# Alerts: /etc/paperbot/live-telegram.env (the live bot's own token and the owners' private chats), loaded after this
# file by the unit, sets them; nothing to write here when that file has them. Without that file, remove the "#" and
# write the token and the chat ids (never leave a chat line empty: keep it commented out instead).
#TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_WARN=
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_INFO=
